  "claim": "Wayne Pride was the opening act for in early 2004 for the singer nicknamed \"Gentle Giant\". Gentle Giants originally sang a song included as the third single in Mel McDaniel 1980 album \"I'm Countryfied\"",
  "evidencia": "Page: Louisiana Saturday Night. Sentence: \"Louisiana Saturday Night\" is a song written by Bob McDill and recorded by American country music artist, Mel McDaniel.\nPage: Louisiana Saturday Night. Sentence: It was released in March 1981 as the third single from McDaniel's 1980 album, \"I'm Countryfied\".\nPage: Louisiana Saturday Night. Sentence: The song was originally sung by Don Williams.\nPage: Don Williams. Sentence: Don Williams (born Donald Ray Williams; May 27, 1939 – September 8, 2017) was an American country singer, songwriter, and 2010 inductee to the Country Music Hall of Fame.\nPage: Don Williams. Sentence: His straightforward yet smooth bass-baritone voice, soft tones, and imposing build earned him the nickname: \"Gentle Giant\" of country music.\nPage: Wayne Pride. Sentence: He was the opening act for Don Williams in early 2004.",
